{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1960495","formula":"C₂₇H₃₅N₅O₇S","hill":"C27H35N5O7S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":27.0,"H":35.0,"N":5.0,"O":7.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Met-enkephalin","ru":"Мет-энкефалин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Met-enkephalin, also known as metenkefalin (INN), sometimes referred to as opioid growth factor (OGF), is a naturally occurring, endogenous opioid peptide that has opioid effects of a relatively short duration. It is one of the two forms of enkephalin, the other being leu-enkephalin. The enkephalins are considered to be the primary endogenous ligands of the δ-opioid receptor, due to their high potency and selectivity for the site over the other endogenous opioids.","ru":"Мет-энкефалин, также известный, как опиоидный фактор роста (англ. opioid growth factor сокр. OGF ) — органическое соединение, являющееся одним из важнейших представителей класса энкефалинов, особых нейропептидов, являющихся эндогенными лигандами-агонистами опиоидных рецепторов."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":443363,"mass":573.7,"charge":0,"smiles":"CSCC[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC1=CC=CC=C1)NC(=O)CNC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CC2=CC=C(C=C2)O)N","inchikey":"YFGBQHOOROIVKG-FKBYEOEOSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-[[(2S)-2-[[2-[[2-[[(2S)-2-amino-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl]amino]acetyl]amino]acetyl]amino]-3-phenylpropanoyl]amino]-4-methylsulfanylbutanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"443363","atoms":75,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.723,"y":0.358,"z":4.562,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.785,"y":2.086,"z":4.025,"el":"S"},{"x":-4.185,"y":1.849,"z":2.259,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.988,"y":1.315,"z":1.474,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.302,"y":1.127,"z":-0.016,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.344,"y":2.486,"z":-0.731,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.195,"y":3.349,"z":-0.572,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.298,"y":